14 sign-vs-local-quality\n\n**Setup**: Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct on ALFWorld, RAGEN framework, 2×A6000, GRPO group size 8, lr 5e-6.\n\n**Paper structure**: Abstract, Intro, Related Work, Section 3 (Problem Analysis), Section 4 (Method: Episode-level GRPO), Section 5 (Experiments: convergence, multi-seed, h-sweep, GAE comparison, per-task, verification ablation), Section 6 (Preliminary: selective verification), Discussion, Conclusion.\n\n## Experiment Design Context\n\nThe paper's imagined experiment plan included these experiments that were NOT executed:\n- ScienceWorld transfer (not executed — resource/time constraints)\n- 7B model scaling verification (not executed — GPU constraints)\n\nThese that were executed but presented as preliminary/weak:\n- Selective verification (B-IAVR): 28% verification reduction, weak Pareto performance\n- Entropy-controlled action-change analysis: partial correlation drops to 0.08, p=0.12 (not significant)\n- Causal intervention: p=0.04, weak effect\n- ARES reproduction: B-IAVR doesn't dominate ARES\n\n## Your Review Task\n\nEvaluate the paper on these dimensions with detailed justification:\n\n### 1. Methodological Soundness\n- Is the dual mechanism analysis (policy info loss + sign misattribution) well-formulated and rigorously verified?\n- Is the mathematical formulation in Section 3 correct? Are there gaps?\n- Is the empirical verification (Table 1) convincing? Is r=0.87 strong enough to claim \"predominantly determined by\"?\n- Is the \"necessary minimum\" / \"sufficient improvement\" framing of episode-level vs GAE justified by the data?\n\n### 2. Experimental Rigor\n- Are the experiments sufficient to support the claims?\n- Multi-seed (5 seeds for main, 3 seeds for ablations) — adequate?\n- Is the h-sweep design appropriate? Are 15 training steps enough?\n- Is the GAE comparison fair (same training steps, different cost)?\n- Statistical significance: are proper tests used? CI reported?\n- ALFWorld-only: how much does single-environment limit the claims?\n- 1.5B model only: how much does single-scale limit generalizability?\n\n### 3. Experimental Coverage vs Plan\n- The paper covers: convergence, multi-seed, h-sweep, GAE comparison, per-task, verification ablation, selective verification (preliminary)\n- Missing: ScienceWorld, 7B scaling\n- Are the executed experiments sufficient for the diagnostic claims?\n\n### 4. Presentation Quality\n- Are tables clear and informative?\n- Is the narrative coherent across sections?\n- Any data that contradicts claims but isn't discussed?\n\n### 5. Weaknesses (be specific)\nList concrete weaknesses with severity (minor/moderate/major).\n\n### 6. Questions for Authors\nList 3-5 specific questions you would ask.\n\n### 7. Overall Assessment\n- Score (1-6 scale: 1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Weak Reject, 4=Weak Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept)\n- Confidence (1-5: 1=low, 5=expert)\n- One-paragraph summary justification\n\nFormat your review clearly with headers. Be rigorous but fair — this is positioned as a diagnostic/analysis paper, not a SOTA-chasing paper.","uuid":"7791d44b-20ec-4a17-8acb-12dc833a55d1","session_id":"c1b768d7-c0d6-42f3-9a34-70349ec3e8c8"}
